[{:adr/id 2799006310, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-6310 — Subsistence Crop Farmers Household Record-Keeping/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/status :accepted, :adr/date "2026-07-18", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6310], :adr/references [2607121000], :adr/related ["adr-2799007111-cloud-itonami-isco-7111-house-builders-coverage" "adr-2799008341-cloud-itonami-isco-8341-farm-forestry-plant-operators-coverage"], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-6310, :actor/name "Subsistence Crop Farming Household Coordination Practice", :actor/domain :agriculture/subsistence-crop-farming-household-coordination, :actor/isco-08 "6310", :actor/wave 3, :actor/robotics? true, :actor/coordination? true, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-farm-operation :flag-livelihood-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-livelihood-concern], :actor/hard-checks [:no-farmer :no-plot :no-actuation :unknown-op :scope-excluded-action], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-planting-decision :finalize-harvest-timing-decision :proceed-with-planting-decision :proceed-with-harvest-decision :override-farmer-crop-judgment], :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["proceed with the planting decision" "proceed with the harvest decision" "proceed with the harvest timing decision" "finalize the planting decision" "finalize the harvest timing decision" "override the farmer's crop judgment" "override the farmer's judgment" "override farmer crop judgment" "override farmer judgment"], :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 300}", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :registry/maturity :implemented, :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6310", :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-6310", :test/counts "{:total 23, :assertions 50, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :farmer-verification :plot-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation :livelihood-concern-always-escalate], :test/simulator :subsistencefarm.actor-test, :db/id -1, :adr/body "# ADR 2799006310: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 6310 Subsistence Crop Farmers household record-keeping/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 6310\n-- Subsistence Crop Farmers** only, Wave3 (production/trades, sub-major\n`63` under `kotoba.occupation.wave`) of the rollout.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"6310\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"6310\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Subsistence Crop Farmers\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6310` (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `6310` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nSubsistence Crop Farmers grow crops primarily for household\nconsumption, not commercial sale -- this carries a distinct\nlivelihood-vulnerability dimension on top of the standard agricultural\nphysical-safety hazards other cloud-itonami agriculture verticals\ncarry: a crop-failure risk here threatens the household's own food\nsecurity directly, not merely a commercial outcome. The controlling\nconstraint for this vertical is that the closed op allowlist must\nNEVER include any op that directly finalizes a planting/harvest-timing\ndecision or overrides the farmer's own judgment about their\nhousehold's crops -- those decisions must always be a hard permanent\nblock or an always-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible. This actor\nis deliberately scoped to FARM RECORD-KEEPING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION\nONLY -- it never makes agronomic decisions itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance + scope-exclusion\nsafety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7111)\n(House Builders: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor` split,\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, closest standard module\nshape) -- cloned and read in full in this session and used as the\ndirect structural template (farmer/plot provenance in place of\nbuilder/site provenance, `:flag-livelihood-concern` in place of\n`:flag-safety-concern` as the always-escalate op).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6310` as an OSS household\nrecord-keeping/logistics-coordination actor for subsistence crop\nfarmers, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Subsistence Farm Advisor\n⊣ SubsistenceFarmGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family), with\nan independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **farm record-keeping/logistics coordination\nONLY, never direct agronomic-decision authority** -- it must NEVER be\ndesigned to exercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\nplanting/harvest-timing decision, or any override of the farmer's own\njudgment about their household's crops. These are not merely gated\nbehind escalation -- they are structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- planting/harvest/yield record data logging\n- `:schedule-farm-operation` -- household labor/task scheduling\n  proposal\n- `:flag-livelihood-concern` -- surface a crop-failure-risk/\n  food-security concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- seeds/tools procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nplanting/harvest-timing agronomic decision or a farmer-crop-judgment\noverride. These are **structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-planting-decision` cannot even be proposed by the reference\nmock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only ever emit one\nof the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a forged proposal, a\nfuture LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever produced such an op, the\ngovernor's closed-allowlist HARD check (`:unknown-op`) rejects it\nunconditionally and permanently. A second, independent HARD check\n(`:scope-excluded-action`) names five concretely-forbidden ops\n(`subsistencefarm.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-planting-decision`, `:finalize-harvest-timing-decision`,\n`:proceed-with-planting-decision`, `:proceed-with-harvest-decision`,\n`:override-farmer-crop-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is verified\nby dedicated unit tests\n(`subsistencefarm.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-planting-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-harvest-timing-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-planting-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-harvest-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-farmer-crop-judgment`), plus\ntwo full-graph-run tests\n(`subsistencefarm.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`,\n`.../holds-an-override-farmer-crop-judgment-proposal`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Farmer unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered farmer record (`:no-farmer`). Never trusts\n   the proposal's own claim of who the farmer is.\n2. **Plot unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an independently\n   registered farm plot (`:no-plot`). Together with check 1, this\n   directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a farmer/plot\n   record must be independently verified/registered before any\n   action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the five\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with or\n   finalizing a planting/harvest-timing decision, or overriding the\n   farmer's own crop judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT block\n   (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on content --\n   defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if a future\n   change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based rejection still\n   independently blocks planting/harvest-finalization/farmer-override\n   language wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-livelihood-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless\n  of confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a crop-failure-risk/\n  food-security observation -- it never resolves the concern itself,\n  and the robot's role ends at \"here is the livelihood-risk data,\"\n  never \"here is what I recommend doing about the household's crops.\"\n  This op can NEVER be auto-commit-eligible, per the subsistence-\n  farming livelihood-vulnerability dimension: a crop failure here\n  threatens the household's own food security, unlike a purely\n  commercial outcome in the reference vertical.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (300, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. The threshold is set at\n  household scale (lower than the reference vertical's commercial\n  building-materials threshold of 2000), reflecting a subsistence\n  household's typical seeds/tools procurement budget. This is an\n  ESCALATION, not a hard block, per the task's explicit domain design:\n  an over-threshold supply order is not itself a livelihood-threatening\n  agronomic decision, unlike a planting/harvest-finalization or\n  farmer-judgment-override attempt, which is why it is handled by a\n  different mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"planting\", \"harvest\", \"crop\", \"farmer\") can accidentally match\ninside the mock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate\nproposal, self-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly\nthe risk this vertical's own vocabulary (a household coordination\nactor working adjacent to planting/harvest work necessarily discusses\nthose concepts to do its scheduling/logging job) could trigger if\nphrased carelessly.\n`subsistencefarm.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is phrased\nexclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"proceed with the\nplanting decision\", \"finalize the harvest timing decision\", \"override\nthe farmer's crop judgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example\nphrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`subsistencefarm.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for farmer ...\", \"scheduled farm operation for planting\ntask ...\", \"... routed for human review\") WITHOUT containing any of\nthe full finalization-action phrases, so the regression test is a\ngenuine stress test of the bare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not\na vacuous pass. Green on first run in this session -- the\nscope-exclusion self-trip guard itself was never tripped during\ndevelopment.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"6310\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-6310` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-6310`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 23 tests, 50 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-planting-decision` or\n  `:approve-harvest-timing-decision` that is merely gated behind an\n  always-escalate list: rejected outright per the task's explicit\n  domain-design guidance -- an always-escalate op still means the\n  *capability* to finalize a planting/harvest-timing decision exists\n  in the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a\n  decision this severe (household food-security risk from crop\n  failure), the capability itself must not exist. The only op related\n  to livelihood-risk escalation is `:flag-livelihood-concern`, which\n  surfaces the need for human/household attention and never itself\n  decides, authorizes, or defers a planting/harvest decision for later\n  automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the\n  reference's cost-ceiling HARD-check alternatives considered in prior\n  ADRs): rejected per the task's explicit domain design -- an\n  over-threshold seeds/tools supply order is not itself a\n  livelihood-threatening agronomic decision, so it is handled as a\n  soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the\n  planting/harvest-finalization/farmer-judgment-override class is a\n  hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"planting\" \"harvest\"\n  \"crop\" \"farmer\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip\n  bug class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for\n  this exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses\n  planting/harvest/crop concepts to do its scheduling/logging job, so\n  a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own legitimate\n  proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale text that\n  deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Merging `farmer` and `plot` into a single entity (only checking one\n  provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered farmer AND independently-registered plot)\n  matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"farmer/plot record must be\n  independently verified/registered before any action\" and the\n  established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with\n  two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- planting/harvest/yield record data\n   logging only. Requires an independently registered farmer AND plot\n   (`:no-farmer`/`:no-plot`). Not a planting/harvest-timing agronomic\n   decision or a farmer-judgment override in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-farm-operation`** -- household labor/task scheduling\n   proposal only. Cannot carry a planting/harvest-timing decision\n   (structurally absent from the op's field shape; any such attempt\n   via free text is caught by the `:scope-excluded-action` content\n   check). Does not authorize, finalize, or draw any conclusion about\n   when to plant or harvest a specific crop -- it is a\n   calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-livelihood-concern`** -- surfaces a crop-failure-risk/\n   food-security concern to a human/household member for review;\n   ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence level, NEVER\n   auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through which a\n   livelihood observation may be surfaced, and it explicitly never\n   resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself -- the farmer reviews\n   and acts entirely on their own authority and judgment about their\n   own household's crops.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- seeds/tools procurement proposal\n   only (item, cost). Not a planting/harvest-timing decision or\n   authorization of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics action,\n   gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 300 always\n   escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na planting/harvest-timing agronomic decision (e.g. deciding when to\nplant or harvest a crop) or an override of the farmer's own judgment\nabout their household's crops -- these categories are structurally\nabsent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist\nitself (`subsistencefarm.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) five\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`subsistencefarm.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`subsistencefarm.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-planting-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-harvest-timing-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-planting-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-harvest-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-farmer-crop-judgment`), and\n(c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`subsistencefarm.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with a planting decision or override the\nfarmer's crop judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`subsistencefarm.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-farmer`).\n"}]
